            <ArticleTitle>Coronary artery bypass grafting nine years after cardiac transplantation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>571-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Angina and increasing exertional dyspnea developed in a 53-year-old man 9 years after cardiac transplantation. Left heart catheterization revealed severe proximal triple coronary artery disease, and he underwent surgical revascularization. Now 18 months after the operation he continues to be free of symptoms.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
